# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the native stage/layer fuzzer.
#
# OpenUSD deliberately keeps process-lifetime singletons that are never freed:
# the TfRegistryManager library state, interned SdfPath nodes and their token
# registry, the TfRegistryInit tables, and the trace event lists. TBB allocates
# some of that state through its own callback machinery. LeakSanitizer reports
# all of it at exit, which is not a defect and cannot be fixed from this
# repository.
#
# Suppress by owning module so a newly reported OpenUSD singleton does not fail
# the gate, while leaks that are genuinely ours - allocated by the fuzz harness
# or by openusd_dotnet without passing through OpenUSD - are still reported.
leak:libusd_ms.so
leak:libtbb
leak:Tf_RegistryManagerImpl
leak:Tf_RegistryInit
